//
// Every nesting form at exactly 300 levels — `crate::limits::LIMIT` — compiles and answers on
// both backends.  Each `+`, `**`, `??` and postfix step is one level, as is each bracket, call,
// block, branch and vector element, so the chains hold 301 operands and the method chain 300
// calls.  Expected values by hand: a nest of 1 stays 1, 300 negations cancel, 301 ones sum to
// 301, every `n` is null so `??` falls through to 7, 300 `.inc()` from 0 is 300, and 1.0 to any
// power is 1.0.  Its refused twin is `an-expression-nested-past-the-bound-is-refused.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — it pins the limit's lower side; a bound set below 300 fails it with
//   the refusal.

